  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=5u-3v-2,\\,y=2u+v+7\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ a & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v-2 \\\\ 2u+v+7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v-2 \\\\ 2u+v+7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+1+(-2)=1.\n$$",
